479 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Flowchart illustrating a data processing pipeline. Data matrices are first split into smaller matrices, then undergo linear projection and position embedding. They are processed by a transformer, followed by an LSTM layer, resulting in a softmax output.) /K 519 0 R /P 226 0 R /Pg 218 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
480 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Bar chart showing the number of samples in thousands across different durations: 300 to 500 ms, 300 to 700 ms, 300 to 1000 ms, and 500 to 1000 ms. Three categories are represented: stable \(blue\), upward \(orange\), and downward \(green\). Stable has the highest count in the 300 to 500 ms range, upward leads in the 300 to 700 ms and 300 to 1000 ms ranges, and downward has slightly higher values in the 300 to 1000 ms and 500 to 1000 ms ranges. A table below presents the exact figures for each category and duration.) /K 520 0 R /P 226 0 R /Pg 220 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
